When a candidate source’s fetch fails after the source was removed
from its media element, or moved out of it, Ladybird now fires no error
event at it, and still fires one at a candidate moved within the
element. Run in Chrome 157.0.8103.79, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5:
Chrome fires none in any of the three cases, WebKit fires none for the
removal (and has no moveBefore() for the moves), and Firefox fires one
in all three. So Ladybird matches Chrome for the removal and the move
out, and Firefox for the move within the element, where the spec keeps
the source as the candidate.
